---
description: Keep BlomboUI lightweight. Simple structure, small single-purpose files, cleaner when it is clearly better, still easy to extend later.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Lightweight and simple

BlomboUI stays a thin GUI over ComfyUI. Prefer the smallest design that is still easy to change next month.

## Structure

- Keep the tree obvious: install launchers, backend, frontend, Comfy as the generation backend.
- Backend lives at `app/backend/src/` with `api/` (routes), `features/` (`service.py` + `scripts/`), `shared/`, `infrastructure/` (Comfy client + storage), and `bootstrap/` (install-time env files).
- Frontend lives at `app/frontend/src/` with `app/` (shell + router), `views/` (`*View.tsx` + `panels/<region>/`), `components/` (`primitives/`, `controls/`, `layout/`, `composites/`), `theme/`, `lib/`, and `stores/`.
- `views/settings/panels/content/sections/other/PrimitivesSection.tsx` is the live catalog of existing controls. Check it and `style-frontend.mdc` / `dev-frontend.mdc` before adding UI.
- Do not add layers, services, or "core" packages for one caller.
- A new feature is usually one small module plus the screen that uses it — not a new architecture.

## File size and one job

- One file, one job. If you cannot name the file in a few words, split it.
- Soft limit **500 lines**. If a file is heading there, extract a sibling — do not grow a god file.
- Split by responsibility (`jobs.py`, `comfy.py`), not by ceremony (`JobServiceFactory`).

```text
❌  api.py (routes + sqlite + Comfy websocket + image import)
✅  main.py (app shell)  api/routes/  features/  infrastructure/comfy  infrastructure/storage
```

## Cleaner when it is clearly better

- If the same thing can be done with less code, fewer types, or a straighter data flow, do that.
- Delete indirection that does not earn its keep. Do not "simplify" by rewriting working code into a new pattern.
- Match what is already here (FastAPI, small React screens, zustand). No extra framework.
- Keep `infrastructure/storage/user.py`, `infrastructure/storage/cache.py`, and `infrastructure/storage/cache_gallery.py` separate; they own different SQLite files. Table access goes through `infrastructure/storage/repositories/`.
- Keep `bootstrap/env.py` path/YAML helpers separate from API runtime helpers in `config.py` / `shared/dirs.py`.

## Robust later

- Robust means obvious seams and stable names, not speculative flexibility.
- Put I/O at the edges (Comfy, disk, HTTP). Keep the middle boring.
- New work should plug in as another small file. If it needs a config system, a plugin loader, or a shared base class "for later", stop.
